ce URL\\nimage_url = image_tag[\\'src\\'] if image_tag else None\\nprint(image_url)\\n``` ', 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}, {'step': 2, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'Address: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Nebel\\nTitle: Carl Nebel - Wikipedia\\nViewport position: Showing page 1 of 3.\\n=======================\\n# Carl Nebel\\n\\nGerman painter\\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Mexico_nebel.jpg/220px-Mexico_nebel.jpg)](/wiki/File:Mexico_nebel.jpg)\\n\\n**Carl Nebel** (18 March 1805 – 4 June 1855) was a [German](/wiki/Germans \"Germans\") engineer, architect and draughtsman,[[1]](#cite_note-thb-1) best known for his detailed paintings and [lithographic prints](/wiki/Lithography \"Lithography\") made from them of the Mexican landscape and people during the battles of the [Mexican–American War](/wiki/Mexican%E2%80%93American_War \"Mexican–American War\").\\n\\nBiography\\n---------\\n\\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=Carl_Nebel&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Biography\")]\\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Nebel_Mexican_War_12_Scott_in_Mexico_City.jpg/220px-Nebel_Mexican_War_12_Scott_in_Mexico_City.jpg)](/wiki/File:Nebel_Mexican_War_12_Scott_in_Mexico_City.jpg)\\n\\nScott\\'s Entry to the [Plaza de la Constitución](/wiki/Z%C3%B3calo \"Zócalo\")\\n\\nNebel was born in [Altona](/wiki/Altona,_Hamburg \"Altona, Hamburg\"), today a part of [Hamburg](/wiki/Hamburg \"Hamburg\"). After studies in [Hamburg](/wiki/Hamburg \"Hamburg\") and Paris, he travelled to [America](/wiki/Americas \"Americas\"),[[1]](#cite_note-thb-1) where he was a resident of [Mexico](/wiki/Mexico \"Mexico\") from 1829 until 1834. In 1836, he published in Paris his renowned illustrated work on that country—*Voyage pittoresque et archéologique dans la partie la plus intéressante du Méxique*, with 50 [lithographs](/wiki/Lithography \"Lithography\") made from his paintings, twenty of which were hand-colored, 